{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Include fireworks in clean air laws & restrict high-smoke sales",
        "additional_details": "During autumn events like Diwali and Bonfire Night, chemical smoke mixes with fog and stagnant air, trapping PM2.5, sulfur dioxide, and heavy metals at ground level. This creates toxic smog that triggers severe asthma attacks and respiratory distress. Vehicle emissions are regulated in low-emission zones, but pyrotechnic smoke remains unregulated. We call for low-smoke standards in urban areas, council powers during fog, and promotion of drone or laser alternatives.",
        "background": "Amend pyrotechnic regulations to restrict high-smoke fireworks in residential areas. Empower councils to limit consumer fireworks during fog and atmospheric inversions to protect public health and individuals with respiratory conditions like asthma.",
